The exact line where the vulnerability is is:

```c
textlist[i]=(char*)NULL;
```

This line is used to set the i-th element of the textlist array to NULL. However, there is no check to ensure that the array is not already full before this line is executed. If the text is long enough, it could overflow the array, leading to an out-of-bounds access. This could lead to undefined behavior, including memory corruption, or, in the worst case, code execution.

To fix this vulnerability, you should add a check to ensure that the array is not already full before setting the i-th element to NULL. Here is a possible fix:

```c
if (i >= number_lines) {
    // Handle error or exit
}
textlist[i] = (char*)NULL;
```

This will ensure that the array does not overflow and will prevent an out-of-bounds access.

